  "articleBody": "It's easy to overlook roof damage, especially if it's not pouring inside your living room! But catching issues early can save you a ton of hassle and cash down the line. So, when should you pick up the phone for a professional evaluation? Let's talk about some key signals.\n\n### When Professional Guidance Helps\n\n- **After a major storm:** Texas weather can be brutal. If you've just had hail, strong winds, or heavy rains, it's always a good idea to get your roof checked out, even if you don't see immediate leaks. Hail damage, for instance, isn't always obvious from the ground but can compromise your roof's integrity. Discounted Roofing Co. specializes in storm and hail-damage assessments.\n- **Visible exterior signs:** Missing shingles, cracked tiles, or sagging spots are clear indicators. Don't ignore those dark streaks or granules in your gutters either; they could mean your roof is aging faster than it should be.\n- **Interior water stains:** Any discoloration on your ceilings or walls, especially in the attic, means water is getting in. This isn't just an aesthetic problem; it can lead to mold and structural damage if not addressed quickly.\n- **Aging roof:** If your roof is approaching 15-20 years old, regular evaluations are a must. Even if it looks okay, age can make materials brittle and less effective at protecting your home.\n- **Pre-purchase or post-purchase home inspection:** A dedicated roof evaluation can uncover issues that a general home inspection might miss, giving you a clearer picture of your investment.\n\nDon't wait for a small problem to become a major headache. An evaluation helps distinguish storm damage from prior issues and can identify hidden problems before they get worse. It’s about protecting your home and giving you peace of mind. If you’re seeing any of these signs, it's time to get a professional to take a look.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}